      {
        "id": 37709,
        "name": "Jigoku Meguri",
        "summary": "Bonze is a Buddhist monk passing through Hell with only his prayer beads to protect him in this horror-themed Arcade platform.\n\nBonze Adventure, or Jigoku Meguri (\"Hell Tour\"), is an Arcade platformer featuring the eponymous Buddhist monk Bonze has he makes his way through the Shinto/Buddhist equivalent of Hell. He is beset by demons and yokai from all sides but is able to exorcise them with his prayer beads, which are thrown outwards with a bouncing motion.\n\nJigoku Meguri was first released to the Arcade in 1988 and later saw a Japan-only PC Engine port in 1990.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co6boq.jpg",
